    <header class=3D"hero">
      <div class=3D"eyebrow">Harmony-remote-assistant =C2=B7 project log =
=C2=B7 12 Nov 2026</div>
      <h1>The Harmony 600, readable without Logitech</h1>
      <p class=3D"lede">The remote's configuration is backed up over USB an=
d read back locally into its devices, IR codes, button names and activities=
, with no Logitech software or server involved. Nothing has been written to=
 the remote. This page records how, what came out, and what comes next.</p>
    </header>

    <section id=3D"status">
      <h2>Status</h2>
      <div class=3D"status">
        <div><span class=3D"chip ok">Done</span><b>Backup</b><span>666,177 =
bytes read off the remote through libconcord, with its checksums.</span></d=
iv>
        <div><span class=3D"chip ok">Done</span><b>Local reader</b><span>Af=
terglow imports the backup: 3 devices, all 175 IR codes, 2 activities.</spa=
n></div>
        <div><span class=3D"chip ok">Done</span><b>Verified</b><span>35 of =
36 named TV keys send Samsung's own code for that name.</span></div>
        <div><span class=3D"chip warn">Waiting</span><b>Building new config=
s</b><span>harmony-explorations can do it; running it needs your permission=
 and your device models.</span></div>
        <div><span class=3D"chip risk">Risk</span><b>Logitech's service</b>=
<span>MyHarmony still answers today. The older service closed on 28 May 202=
5.</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"route">
      <h2>How it was done</h2>
      <p class=3D"sub">In order. Every USB step only read.</p>
      <ol class=3D"steps">
        <li><div><b>Took MyHarmony apart</b><span>A 2013 browser shell runn=
ing a Silverlight app from Logitech's servers, which drives the remote thro=
ugh a USB plugin and about 230 protocol templates.</span></div></li>
        <li><div><b>Assessed going offline</b><span>Four proposals; the blo=
cker was the server that compiles devices and activities into the remote's =
configuration file.</span></div></li>
        <li><div><b>Backed up with Afterglow</b><span>Its libconcord, taken=
 from the checksum-verified Windows release, identified the remote and read=
 <code>/cfg/usercfg</code>. No driver was changed.</span></div></li>
        <li><div><b>Found the format</b><span>The file is the Harmony One's=
 <code>GSPM</code> image with a different base, index and constant; the One=
's checksum matches exactly.</span></div></li>
        <li><div><b>Taught Afterglow the 600</b><span>A read-only profile a=
nd backend: section mapping, command objects, the 54-key table, the LCD fon=
t, page labels and activity names.</span></div></li>
        <li><div><b>Evaluated a builder</b><span>harmony-explorations build=
s 600 configurations from a recipe and has run one on a real 600.</span></d=
iv></li>
        <li><div><b>Saved and documented</b><span>Everything is in local gi=
t repositories, with a process document and a format document.</span></div>=
</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"remote">
      <h2>What is on the remote</h2>
      <p class=3D"sub">Harmony 600, skin 71, architecture 14, firmware 0.3,=
 board 1.1.0.</p>
      <div class=3D"tbl"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Device</th><th>Commands</th><th>Named</th><th>Exampl=
es of names read</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>TV <span class=3D"caption">(Samsung)</span></td><td class=
=3D"num">71</td><td class=3D"num">55</td><td><span class=3D"names">VolumeUp=
, Number0=E2=80=939, Red=E2=80=A6Blue, Menu, Guide, SRC, 3D, HDMI1- CCTV, H=
DMI2- AVR, HDMI- ARC, HDMI3, Subtitles</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>AVR</td><td class=3D"num">54</td><td class=3D"num">52</td=
><td><span class=3D"names">Bluetooth, Radio, Internet Radio, Online Music, =
Media Player, TV Audio, CD, CBL/SAT, Bluray/DVD, Game, Aux, USB</span></td>=
</tr>
          <tr><td>HiFi <span class=3D"caption">(Panasonic-type IR)</span></=
td><td class=3D"num">50</td><td class=3D"num">20</td><td><span class=3D"nam=
es">Power Toggle, Input Radio, Input Cd/Usb/Aux, D.Bass, Sound Mode, Preset=
 Next, Timer, Sleep, Setup</span></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <div class=3D"tbl"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Activity</th><th>Starts</th><th>Keys go to</th></tr>=
</thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Muzica</td><td>AVR on, HiFi off</td><td>AVR</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Tiv=C3=B9</td><td>TV on</td><td>TV</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <p class=3D"caption">Commands still numbered (16 TV, 2 AVR, 30 HiFi) =
are used by no key and no page, so the file gives them no name.</p>
    </section>

