      <p class=3D"caption"><code>python tools/lifeboat_read.py --dlls vendo=
r/afterglow-dlls</code>, then <code>python tools/read_600_config.py backups=
/&lt;folder&gt;/config.ezhex</code>. MyHarmony must be closed first.</p>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"format">
      <h2>The 600 format</h2>
      <p class=3D"sub">Measured on this remote's backup. Full detail is in =
<code>afterglow/docs/harmony_600/README.md</code>.</p>
      <div class=3D"tbl"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Harmony One</th><th>Harmony 600</th></=
tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Magic, end marker, checksum</td><td><code>GSPM</code>, <c=
ode>PTYY</code>, XOR lanes <code>0x21</code>/<code>0x43</code></td><td>the =
same</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Pointer base</td><td class=3D"num">0x040000</td><td class=
=3D"num">0x030000</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Header constant</td><td class=3D"num">0x1600</td><td clas=
s=3D"num">0x1400</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Section index</td><td>20 slots, slot 8 absent</td><td>18 =
slots; One 9=E2=80=9318 are 600 8=E2=80=9317, no touch section</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Command object</td><td><code>7D 7C</code></td><td><code>7=
F 7D 7C</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Screen slot</td><td>template, key register, program</td><=
td>key register, program</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Keys</td><td>40, scan 1=E2=80=9340</td><td>54, scan 1=E2=
=80=9354, own numbering</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"builder">
      <h2>Building configs</h2>
      <p>harmony-explorations (MIT) builds a whole 600 configuration from a=
 recipe of devices and activities, without any Logitech file, and has writt=
en one to a real 600 that ran it. 16 of its 68 requirements for the 600 are=
 proven by tests, among them build, verified write, and backup and restore.=
 Still open: turning an existing configuration into an editable recipe, cat=
alogue search, and a written procedure for writing to a new owner's remote.=
</p>
      <p>To rebuild this remote's setup it needs a catalogue entry per devi=
ce. The configuration stores no make or model, so those have to come from M=
yHarmony or from matching the recovered IR codes against the IR archive (27=
6,000 devices, CC0, already downloaded).</p>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"saved">
      <h2>What is saved</h2>
      <p class=3D"sub">All local; nothing is pushed anywhere.</p>
      <div class=3D"tbl"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Where</th><th>Branch</th><th>What</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>Harmony-remote-assistant</code></td><td><code>work/=
harmony-600</code></td><td>backup, tools, docs, MyHarmony research text, th=
e saved pages</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>afterglow/</code></td><td><code>harmony-600-readonl=
y</code></td><td>the 600 profile, backend, glyph table and format document<=
/td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>vendor/afterglow-dlls/</code></td><td>on disk</td><=
td>libconcord for Windows, with <code>SOURCE.txt</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>research/myharmony/</code></td><td>text in git, bin=
aries on disk</td><td>MyHarmony packages, assemblies, templates, scripts</t=
d></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <ul class=3D"clean">
        <li><code>docs/afterglow-harmony-600.md</code>: the whole process, =
step by step and reproducible</li>
        <li><code>docs/harmony-explorations-evaluation.md</code>: the build=
er evaluation</li>
        <li><code>afterglow/docs/harmony_600/README.md</code>: the format, =
as Afterglow documentation</li>
      </ul>
      <p class=3D"caption"><span class=3D"chip risk">Keep a copy</span> Cop=
y <code>backups/</code> off this computer. It lists what is set up in a hom=
e, so keep it private.</p>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"next">
      <h2>Your decisions</h2>
      <div class=3D"cards">
        <article class=3D"card ask">
          <span class=3D"chip warn">Needs approval</span>
          <h3>Run the builder</h3>
          <p>Installing harmony-explorations' dependencies runs third-party=
 code, so it needs your permission.</p>
          <pre class=3D"cmd">cd harmony-explorations
npx pnpm@11.20.0 install --frozen-lockfile</pre>
        </article>
        <article class=3D"card ask">
          <span class=3D"chip warn">Needs input</span>
          <h3>Device models</h3>
          <p>The make and model of the TV, the AVR and the HiFi, as MyHarmo=
ny lists them. Or ask for a search of the IR archive by the recovered codes=
.</p>
        </article>
        <article class=3D"card">
          <span class=3D"chip ok">Optional</span>
          <h3>Contribute to Afterglow</h3>
          <p>The 600 backend reuses the One's reader, which Afterglow's rem=
ovability rule forbids. A copy or a shared module would fix it; that choice=
 is the maintainers'.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class=3D"caption">Nothing will be written to the remote without yo=
ur explicit approval, and only after a fresh backup.</p>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"pages">
      <h2>Related pages</h2>
      <ul class=3D"clean">
        <li><a href=3D"https://claude.ai/artifact/19NR3pGqSGTQSFSHYc7ibq">M=
yHarmony Teardown</a>: how the MyHarmony software works</li>
        <li><a href=3D"https://claude.ai/artifact/5DPQUGMHRKbXDuN4x95nBg">H=
armony Offline Plan</a>: the four offline proposals, the USB simulator and =
the related projects</li>
        <li><a href=3D"https://github.com/harmonic-afterglow/afterglow">Aft=
erglow</a> =C2=B7 <a href=3D"https://github.com/dannybloe/harmony-explorati=
ons">harmony-explorations</a> =C2=B7 <a href=3D"https://github.com/pickysys=
admin/logitech-harmony-ir-archive">IR archive</a> =C2=B7 <a href=3D"https:/=
/github.com/jaymzh/concordance">Concordance</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <span>Every figure on this page was measured on this remote's backup =
on 11=E2=80=9312 November 2026.</span>
      <span>Prepared with Claude. Nothing was written to the remote.</span>
    </footer>
  </main>
